configd (2.12.2danos7) unstable; urgency=medium

  * session: when a P2 or P4 test pause point holds, it now also writes a seam
    marker file <control dir>/state/<seam>-<component>-<seq>.hit (key=value
    lines: seam, component, kind, seq, pid, call_err, at). call_err is the
    component's reply for P4 ("<nil>" = it answered successfully) and
    "not_sent" for P2, so a test image can tell which seam configd stopped at,
    and that the component had answered, without journald (which does not
    survive under TCG).
  * Still off by default and still free when off: it needs DANOS_TEST_HOOKS=1
    in configd's environment AND a control file naming the component, and with
    the variable unset the pause points remain a nil check (no stat, no open,
    no extra system call). state/ is created by hand on a test image only; if
    it is missing nothing is written. The file is written to a temporary name
    and renamed; a failure is one warning and the commit continues. Nothing is
    written to commit-state.json, and the markers are never removed here.
  * Tests for the marker (P2, P4 with and without an error, rename and create
    failure, missing directory) and for the zero-call case.

 -- i-danos dev <dev@i-danos.dev>  Mon, 26 Oct 2026 22:18:43 -0700

